From 9f8ba59fbfa7ac3d452c2ee045a587f5502ba362 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 23:31:37 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 072/118] dns: test the decisions of the provider DNS fallback

No test called exchangeWithFallback, the function that decides who answers a query and
what a failure does to the server: the tests covered the parts around it (which servers
qualify, the parsing of the netifd dump, the race of the provider's servers, the TTL cap,
the log texts).

Add tests that drive it through a DNS transport answered by the test and a provider that
is a resolver on loopback, with the list of provider servers set, so that ubus is never
run: two failures in a row set the server aside and the provider answers with a capped
TTL; an answer of the server between failures clears the count; a query given up by its
caller counts nothing; the probe of a server set aside, its interval, and the return to
the server; a SERVFAIL replaced by the provider's answer or kept when the provider has no
better one; the provider failing twice in a row; a server set aside when the provider
fails too; no provider known; a server that does not qualify. The timeout of the server
is tested once with the real 3.5 s. Client.exchangeTransport is tested with and without
the fallback.
